  "summary": "Malicious code in bigops-umf-statist (npm)",
  "details": "On require, the package executes a bundled dropper (_runtime.js) that fingerprints the platform/arch and downloads a second-stage binary over HTTPS from Cloudflare Workers endpoints oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev, and oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev (paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, /pkg/package.exe), with a DNS-TXT chunked fallback from the *.dl[.]wel1[.]ru domain (c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru observed). The downloaded payload is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003chex\u003e (or dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe under TEMP on Windows), made executable, and launched detached via /bin/sh -c \"\u003cpath\u003e \u0026\" (cmd.exe /c start /b on Windows). Execution is throttled by a /tmp/.analytics_state lock file.",
